What it does: the component is almost silent inside a document, but fires at the
first token of each document in a packed row (the token right after <|endoftext|>,
or the first token of a row). There the token has no earlier context, so its
activation is fixed by the token itself. The size depends on what kind of text the
token opens:
  - a code or markup opener (#, //, /*, triple quotes, <!, --, import, package, #include,
    const, class, ...) gives a strong positive value (about 5);
  - a space-led fragment, a digit, or punctuation gives a moderate positive value
    (about 1.5 to 2.2), since the document starts mid-text or in a list/number;
  - a capitalised word at the start of a document (a title or prose opening) and
    chat-template tokens give slightly negative values.
