Leading NUL, HTML declaration punctuation, and opening function parameters
have strong positive estimates. Smaller opening estimates depend on white
space, digits, sentence punctuation, quotes, and word-fragment shape.
An uninterrupted repetition of the first token keeps its opening estimate.
Elsewhere there are small formatting and conversation-marker biases, plus
adjustments for dictionary adjective/adverb senses (not contextual POS).
All opening state resets at a new packed document. The coefficients summarize
training observations; token-specific lexical variation is left unmodeled.
