Negative responses mark month names, spaces introducing dates/numbers, and
especially the last digit of two-digit minutes/seconds (strongest for 00/30).
Smaller responses cover date ranges, year prefixes, East Asian calendar/time
units, decimal zeros and paired middle dots. Unrecognized text gets zero.
The carry is reset at document boundaries; this is not a calendar parser.
